3.037 1.505 4.166.645 1.102-.833 1.344-2.204.672-4.166l-5.618-16.718 14.353-10.32c1.666-1.183 2.338-2.42 1.908-3.764-.43-1.29-1.693-1.935-3.763-1.908l-17.605.108-5.348-16.8C34.308 4.496 33.34 3.5 31.944 3.5c-1.372 0-2.34.995-2.984 2.984L23.61 23.283l-17.605-.108c-2.07-.027-3.333.618-3.763 1.908-.457 1.344.242 2.58 1.909 3.763l14.352 10.321-5.617 16.718c-.672 1.962-.43 3.333.672 4.166m3.87-5.321c-.054-.054-.027-.081 0-.242l5.349-15.374c.376-1.049.161-1.882-.78-2.527L8.613 27.341c-.134-.08-.161-.134-.134-.215s.08-.08.242-.08l16.26.295c1.103.027 1.802-.43 2.151-1.532l4.677-15.562c.027-.162.08-.215.134-.215.08 0 .135.053.162.215l4.676 15.562c.35 1.102 1.048 1.559 2.15 1.532l16.261-.296c.162 0 .216 0 .243.081.027.08-.027.134-.135.215l-13.385 9.246c-.94.645-1.156 1.478-.78 2.527l5.35 15.374c.026.161.053.188 0 .242-.055.08-.135.026-.243-.054l-12.928-9.864c-.86-.672-1.855-.672-2.715 0l-12.928 9.864c-.107.08-.188.134-.242.054"></path></svg> </li> </ol></div></div> <div class="review-header svelte-1b79zq6"><time class="date svelte-1b79zq6" datetime="2026-05-23T23:50:50.000Z">May 23</time>  <div class="multiline-clamp svelte-1r39353" style="--mc-lineClamp: var(--defaultClampOverride, 1);" role="text"> <span class="multiline-clamp__text svelte-1r39353"><span class="author svelte-1b79zq6">Thinklazy</span></span> </div></div></div> <div class="content svelte-1b79zq6">  <div class="truncate-wrapper svelte-1mbzmwz"><p data-testid="truncate-text" dir="auto" class="content svelte-1mbzmwz" style="--lines: 3; --line-height: var(--lineHeight, 16); --link-length: 4;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->For our first kid we tried multiple sleep training apps before finding Little Ones. The schedule made sense (we didn’t closely follow the feeding schedule but stuck to the sleeping recommendations) and the guides on gentle sleep training methods based on our comfort level worked when nothing else would! Their guide to taking away the pacifier when the time was right was a life saver for me! I shared this app with many friends and for my 2nd child started from day 1 newborn. Her sleep schedule is predictable, we get to go out with big brother and it’s been such a contrast to the early struggles I remember. The community is helpful on every topic. Only tip to watch out for is that the consulting assumes strictly following schedule. If you are not then the broad tips still help but talking to the consultants doesn’t result in direct help.Highly recommend to know what to do for sleep for your Little One!<!-- HTML_TAG_END --></p> </div>  <div class="developer-response-container svelte-1b79zq6"><span class="developer-response-heading svelte-1b79zq6">Developer Response</span>   <div class="truncate-wrapper svelte-1mbzmwz"><p data-testid="truncate-text" dir="auto" class="content svelte-1mbzmwz" style="--lines: 1; --line-height: var(--lineHeight, 16); --link-length: 4;"><!-- HTML_TAG_START -->Thank you for sharing such a thoughtful review. We’re so glad the schedules, gentle sleep guidance and transition support helped both of your children and gave you more confidence along the way.We also appreciate your feedback about consultant support. Our consultants personalise advice based on the information shared, and the more closely a family is following the schedule framework, the more specific that guidance can often be. We’re grateful for your recommendation and for sharing Little Ones with so many other families. <!-- HTML_TAG_END --></p> </div> </div></div></div>  <dialog data-testid="dialog" class="svelte-1p01z7" id="" aria-hidden="true"><div data-testid="content-modal" class="content-modal-container svelte-1ih6d3u" dir="auto"><div class="button-container svelte-1ih6d3u"><button data-testid="content-modal-close-button" class="close-button svelte-1ih6d3u" type="button" aria-label="Close"><svg width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 18 18" data-testid="content-modal-close-button-svg"><path d="M1.2 18C.6 18 0 17.5 0 16.8c0-.4.1-.6.4-.8l7-7-7-7c-.3-.2-.4-.5-.4